Upstream-Name: q-sunshine-pve
Source: locally built q-sunshine integration tree; Sunshine upstream is https://github.com/LizardByte/Sunshine

Comment:
 The packaged Sunshine executable is built from Sunshine revision
 v2026.830.223700 base 4f39fc116294abf8241bcd30e1b1e23d371e6e7b with the
 q-sunshine ordered QEMU Display1 patch series 0001 through 0008, plus the
 nested Simple-Web-Server request-TLS-handle patch. Patch 0008 is the complete
 transport-only PVE profile: it replaces PIN pairing and host application
 control with system-auth media-lease admission and one fixed QEMU Console
 endpoint. It is pinned as SHA-256
 daa34c1afcc47162762eaeef91f3cc3e2fd507a1e38966a50abb33d5082920b9; its
 nested dependency is pinned as SHA-256
 7c978eaa72a3077fa46f03dc322abd26ac0db0e17cd8be525227cc0976cff2e9.
 Build provenance also pins the LizardByte build-deps release v2026.724.203728
 and the archive digest
 2c27d4694b4ed0e734f497d4bd62f1b3662cbbc4ded2a69f2dc4b703441eebb3.
 Corresponding source is the q-sunshine source tree, the stated Sunshine base
 and patch series, and the upstream build-deps release. The binary's third-party
 notices include FFmpeg, x264, x265, Boost, Opus and their dependencies; its
 GPL-3-or-later combined-work license governs distribution of the executable.

